    title: 'The Silk Road Legacy',
    passage: `The Silk Road was one of history's great cultural highways. Had it not existed, the exchange of ideas between East and West would have been severely limited. If merchants had not travelled such vast distances, we would not enjoy the technological and cultural fusion we see today. One can only imagine what might have been lost were it not for those ancient trade routes. The legacy of the Silk Road reminds us that cooperation across borders has always been essential for human progress. Many historians wish they had more records of those early interactions. If only we could travel back in time to witness those exchanges firsthand. It is time we recognised the importance of preserving this heritage for future generations.`,
